        "code": "# Corrélation : Mortalité adulte vs espérance de vie\npar(bg = \"#1e1e1e\", fg = \"white\", col.axis = \"white\",\n    col.lab = \"white\", col.main = \"white\")\nplot(who$Adult.Mortality, who$Life.expectancy,\n     pch = 16, cex = 0.5,\n     col = ifelse(who$Status == \"Developed\", \"#636EFA80\", \"#EF553B80\"),\n     main = \"Mortalité adulte vs espérance de vie\",\n     xlab = \"Mortalité adulte (pour 1000)\",\n     ylab = \"Espérance de vie (années)\")\nlegend(\"topright\", legend = c(\"Développés\", \"En développement\"),\n       col = c(\"#636EFA\", \"#EF553B\"), pch = 16, text.col = \"white\")",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "r",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<img src=\"blob:http://localhost:8090/4ec50786-4575-4c5d-8a6d-fa65bea341d5\" style=\"max-width: 100%; border-radius: 6px; margin-top: 8px;\">"
      },
      {
        "id": 19,
        "code": "# Modèle linéaire simple : quels facteurs prédisent l'espérance de vie ?\nwho_clean <- na.omit(who[, c(\"Life.expectancy\", \"Schooling\",\n                              \"Adult.Mortality\", \"GDP\", \"BMI\")])\nmodel <- lm(Life.expectancy ~ Schooling + Adult.Mortality + log1p(GDP) + BMI,\n            data = who_clean)\nsummary(model)",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "r",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "\nCall:\nlm(formula = Life.expectancy ~ Schooling + Adult.Mortality + \n    log1p(GDP) + BMI, data = who_clean)\n\nResiduals:\n     Min       1Q   Median       3Q      Max \n-23.9058  -2.3268   0.3833   2.8427  21.6315 \n\nCoefficients:\n                  Estimate Std. Error t value Pr(>|t|)    \n(Intercept)     52.0152589  0.5526905  94.113   <2e-16 ***\nSchooling        1.2286487  0.0420806  29.198   <2e-16 ***\nAdult.Mortality -0.0306218  0.0008859 -34.564   <2e-16 ***\nlog1p(GDP)       0.6985581  0.0673669  10.369   <2e-16 ***\nBMI              0.0580739  0.0061504   9.442   <2e-16 ***\n---\nSignif. codes:  0 ‘***’ 0.001 ‘**’ 0.01 ‘*’ 0.05 ‘.’ 0.1 ‘ ’ 1\n\nResidual standard error: 4.858 on 2453 degrees of freedom\nMultiple R-squared:  0.746,\tAdjusted R-squared:  0.7456 \nF-statistic:  1801 on 4 and 2453 DF,  p-value: < 2.2e-16",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"text-result\" dir=\"ltr\">\nCall:\nlm(formula = Life.expectancy ~ Schooling + Adult.Mortality + \n    log1p(GDP) + BMI, data = who_clean)\n\nResiduals:\n     Min       1Q   Median       3Q      Max \n-23.9058  -2.3268   0.3833   2.8427  21.6315 \n\nCoefficients:\n                  Estimate Std. Error t value Pr(&gt;|t|)    \n(Intercept)     52.0152589  0.5526905  94.113   &lt;2e-16 ***\nSchooling        1.2286487  0.0420806  29.198   &lt;2e-16 ***\nAdult.Mortality -0.0306218  0.0008859 -34.564   &lt;2e-16 ***\nlog1p(GDP)       0.6985581  0.0673669  10.369   &lt;2e-16 ***\nBMI              0.0580739  0.0061504   9.442   &lt;2e-16 ***\n---\nSignif. codes:  0 ‘***’ 0.001 ‘**’ 0.01 ‘*’ 0.05 ‘.’ 0.1 ‘ ’ 1\n\nResidual standard error: 4.858 on 2453 degrees of freedom\nMultiple R-squared:  0.746,\tAdjusted R-squared:  0.7456 \nF-statistic:  1801 on 4 and 2453 DF,  p-value: &lt; 2.2e-16</pre>"
